<div align="center">

# 💡 Smart Street Light System
### 🌙 Intelligent Street Lighting using **LDR + PIR Sensor**

</div>

---

# 🎯 Objective

Develop an intelligent street light system that automatically controls lighting based on **day/night conditions** and **motion detection**, while logging every event with timestamps.

---

# ✨ Features

✅ **Day Mode**
- ☀️ LED remains **OFF**
- 🚫 Motion sensor is ignored

✅ **Night Mode**
- 🌙 Motion detection becomes active

✅ **Motion Detected**
- 💡 LED turns **ON at 100% brightness**

✅ **No Motion for 30 Seconds**
- 🔅 LED automatically dims to **20% brightness**

✅ **Serial Logging**
- 📝 Every event is recorded with a timestamp

---

# 🛠 Components Required

| Component | Quantity |
|:---------|:--------:|
| Arduino Uno | 1 |
| LDR (Photoresistor) | 1 |
| 10kΩ Resistor | 1 |
| PIR Motion Sensor (HC-SR501) | 1 |
| LED | 1 |
| 220Ω Resistor | 1 |
| Breadboard | 1 |
| Jumper Wires | As Required |

---

# 🔌 Circuit Connections

| Component | Arduino Pin |
|:-----------|:-----------:|
| LDR Output | **A0** |
| PIR Output | **D2** |
| LED (+) | **D9 (PWM)** |
| LED (-) | **GND** |

---

# ⚙️ Working Principle

## ☀️ Day Mode

- LDR value is **above the threshold**
- Street light remains **OFF**
- PIR sensor is ignored

---

## 🌙 Night Mode

- LDR value falls **below the threshold**
- Motion detection is enabled

---

## 🚶 Motion Detected

- LED glows at **100% brightness**
- Motion timer starts/reset

---

## 😴 No Motion for 30 Seconds

- LED brightness reduces to **20%**
- Saves power while keeping the street visible

---

# 📟 Sample Serial Output

```text
[00:00:02] EVENT: Night detected - Motion Detection Enabled
[00:00:07] EVENT: Motion detected - LED ON (100%)
[00:00:38] EVENT: No motion for 30 seconds - LED Dimmed (20%)
[00:10:12] EVENT: Daylight detected - Street Light OFF
```

